{{Quote|We are the Mon Cala. The current is against us, but there are no tides we cannot overcome.|Gial Ackbar|<ref name="Star Wars (2015) 49">[[Star Wars (2015) 49|''Star Wars'' (2015) 49]]</ref>}}
The '''Mon Calamari''' (also known as '''Mon Calamarians''') were a [[humanoid]], [[Water|aquatic]] [[species]] native to the [[planet]] of [[Mon Cala]]. They shared their [[Homeworld|home planet]] with the [[Quarren]].

==Biology and appearance==
{{Quote|Ah, is that a grand accelerator? I haven't had an accelerator since my first spawning days!|A Mon Calamari|<ref name="Star Wars (2015) 46">[[Star Wars (2015) 46|''Star Wars'' (2015) 46]]</ref>}}
[[File:MonCalamari-SWE.jpg|thumb|left|180px|Mon Calamari male and female]]
The Mon Calamari were a bipedal, [[Amphibian|amphibious]] [[species]] with high-domed heads, webbed hands and large, goggle-like eyes,<ref name="DB MonCal" /> which stuck out from the sides of their head.<ref name="Worldwide 217">{{InsiderCite|217|Worldwide}}</ref> In addition to being webbed, the Mon Calamari hand presented three suction-cup like holes on its palm, and featured five claw-tipped fingers: one opposable thumb, two long middle fingers, and two very short outer fingers.<ref name="Lair of Grievous" /> Although they were shaped like flippers,<ref name="Water War" /> their feet could nevertheless fit into boots designed for [[humanoid]] feet.<ref name="WotM" /> The [[Gender|females]] were distinguished from the males by their more prominent chest areas.<ref name="SWE">{{SWE|groups|moncalamari|Mon Calamari}}</ref>

The Mon Calamari's skin faded from vibrant in their [[Youngling|youth]] to more worn out as they got older. The individuals that hailed from the colder polar extremes of their planet were noticeably less [[color]]ful than those who came from the tropical zones.<ref name="Much to Learn" /> Prolonged periods without exposure to water would result in a Mon Calamari's skin drying and peeling, creating a painful bleeding that could be exploited as a form of [[torture]]. To survive through droughts, a Mon Calamari's body was able to release a [[hibernation shell]] that covered their body, resulting in the Mon Calamari entering a state of [[biostasis]] through which they would wait out the drought. [[Ecologist]] [[Elping Tsoo]] theorized that the stasis could also be triggered by stress or illness; indeed, the Mon Calamari Ghal Tarpfen found her protective shell released as soon as she was infected by the [[blight]]. During droughts, the Mon Calamari would retreat to the safety of an exposed sea bed, effectively forming a wet, muddy cocoon around themself and the protective shell. As such, the shell retracting over a Mon Calamari in a dry environment could be dangerous and result in suffocation.<ref name="Family Ties">{{InsiderCite|226|Tales from the Occlusion Zone: Family Ties}}</ref>

[[File:Mon_Cal_Hand_Holes.png|thumb|right|The hand of a Mon Calamari]]
Male and female<ref name="AotG">''[[Star Wars: Aliens of the Galaxy]]''</ref> Mon Calamari had [[barbel]]s on their chin. Only having one barbel was an indication of youth, and Mon Calamari gained more as they aged.<ref name="LOG Ep Guide">{{SW|url=series/clone-wars/lair-of-grievous-episode-guide|text="Lair of Grievous" Episode Guide &#124; The Clone Wars}}</ref> Their barbels were also used to help detect pressure changes underwater.<ref name="High Republic Character Encyclopedia">''[[Star Wars: The High Republic Character Encyclopedia]]''</ref> The Mon Calamari were vigorous swimmers and were capable of living underwater for long periods.<ref name="Water War" /> The Mon Calamari [[Reproduction|spawned]] many offspring. For example, [[Raddus]]'s grandchildren numbered in the dozens. However, because not all spawns were expected to come of age, the Mon Calamari felt loss less keenly than humans, who reproduced comparatively rarely and fewer.<ref name="Rogue One novel">[[Rogue One: A Star Wars Story (novelization)|''Rogue One: A Star Wars Story'' novelization]]</ref> The early life of a Mon Calamari was known as their "spawning days."<ref name="Star Wars (2015) 46" />

==Society and culture==
It was common for [[Monarchy|royalty]] or elite members of Mon Cala society to adorn their barbels with ornaments.<ref name="Much to Learn" /> The Mon Calamari were known to find it offensive to sneeze loudly.<ref name="The High Republic: A Test of Courage">''[[The High Republic: A Test of Courage]]''</ref>

==History==
{{Quote|The Mon Calamari make fine ships, but they have proved poor sailors.|Imperial Admiral [[Tyrus Meori]], underestimating the Mon Calamari|<ref name="Star Wars (2015) 49" />}}
[[File:TheLeviathan-MaF.jpg|thumb|left|250px|Legend held that the young Mon Calamari Carus encountered a great leviathan.]]
The Mon Calamari originated on the planet [[Mon Cala]], which they shared with the [[Quarren]] species.<ref name="DB MonCal" /> Both species were influential and most comfortable underwater, where they preferred to build their [[City|cities]] as they preferred to be immersed in liquid.<ref name="VE" /> However, tensions arose between the Quarren and Mon Calamari that resulted in a difficult co-existence.<ref name="Water War" /> Before Mon Cala's environment was able to be influenced by modern technology, the Mon Calamari at times suffered through droughts, which they responded to by entering exposed seabeds and sleeping through the drought in suspended animation.<ref name="Family Ties" /> Legend held that a young Mon Calamari named [[Carus]] ventured into the [[Great Ungeness Trench]] when the Mon Calamari were a fledging species, ignoring the wishes of his friends and family to try and make a name for himself. Within the trench, he uncovered and was killed by a [[Unidentified squid-like creature|squid-like creature]] that shook the ground around his [[Unidentified Mon Calamari city|city]] before it returned to its slumber. Carus's story would be spread as a cautionary tale about why one should not enter the trench, lest the leviathan awaken again.<ref name="Myths & Fables">{{StoryCite|story=The Leviathan|book=Myths & Fables}}</ref>

During the [[High Republic Era]]<ref name="LOTJ">''[[The High Republic: Light of the Jedi]]''</ref> in [[232 BBY]],<ref name="LotJDate">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates the events of ''[[The High Republic: Light of the Jedi]]'' to [[232 BBY]].</ref> [[Supreme Chancellor]] [[Lina Soh]] had a goal of negotiating a new treaty between the Mon Calamari and the Quarren.<ref name="LOTJ" /> During the [[Clone Wars]], the Mon Calamari remained loyal to the [[Galactic Republic]] while the [[Quarren Isolation League]] sided with the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]].<ref name="Water War" /> The [[Mon Calamari Knights]] battled with the Separatist Quarren.<ref name="Tarkin">[[Tarkin (novel)|''Tarkin'']]</ref> Taking advantage of the political crisis, the [[Karkarodon]] Separatist adviser [[Riff Tamson]] stirred up trouble between the two species and funneled Separatist military support to the Quarren chieftain [[Nossor Ri]]. Tensions between the two species reached a climax when the ruling Mon Calamari King [[Yos Kolina]] died under suspicious circumstances. The Quarren quickly contested his son [[Prince]] [[Lee-Char]]'s claim to the throne and demanded to have a greater stake in ruling Mon Cala.<ref name="Water War" />

In response to escalating tensions between the Mon Calamari and Quarren, the Republic dispatched a peace mission consisting of [[Senator]] [[Padmé Amidala Naberrie|Padmé Amidala]] and her [[Jedi]] protector [[Anakin Skywalker]]. Following the failure of mediation, both sides prepared for war. Prince Lee-Char and [[Captain]] [[Gial Ackbar]] prepared the Mon Calamari for war. The Republic also dispatched a company of [[Clone SCUBA trooper]]s under [[Jedi General]] [[Kit Fisto]] and the [[Padawan]] [[Ahsoka Tano]]. Backed by Jedi and Republic reinforcements, the Mon Calamari managed to fight off a Quarren and Separatist assault on [[Coral City|Mon Cala city]]. However, Prince Lee Char and his Jedi and Republic allies were forced to retreat when the Quarren counter-attacked with [[Hydroid Medusa]]ses, gigantic jellyfish with electrified tentacles.<ref name="Water War" />

[[File:Unidentified_Mon_Calamari_soldier.jpg|thumb|right|300px|Mon Calamari soldiers during the Battle of Mon Cala]]
Under the orders of [[Count]] [[Dooku]], the Separatist leader Tamson rounded up the Mon Calamari population in Mon Cala City and shipped them to internment camps. Meanwhile, Prince Lee Char, the surviving Mon Calamari forces and their Republic allies retreated to a few caves near the city.<ref name="Water War" /> Following a failed attempt to smuggle Prince Lee-Char and Senator [[Meena Tills]] offworld, the Prince and his Republic and Jedi allies resolved to continue resisting the Separatist occupiers, who had begun enslaving the Mon Calamari population. Despite the arrival of [[Gungan]] reinforcements from Naboo, the Quarren and their Separatist allies succeeded in capturing most of the Mon Calamari and Republic/Jedi resistance with the exception of Prince Lee Char and Ahsoka.<ref name="Gungan Attack">{{TCW|Gungan Attack}}</ref>

Prince Lee-Char decided to rally Mon Calamari prisoners and to win the Quarren over in order to drive out the Separatist invaders. While attempting to rally prisoners at a Mon Calamari prison camp, he was captured by Separatist forces but secured an audience with Riff Tamson. By this stage, Tamson had strained relations with his Quarren allies by planning to crown himself as the new ruler of Mon Cala. Tamson sentenced Prince Lee-Char to [[death]] but his plans were sabotaged by the Quarren chieftain Nossor Ri, who experienced a change in heart and ordered his followers to support Ackbar and the Mon Calamari. Together, the Mon Calamari, their former Quarren foes, the Republic, Jedi, and the Gungans succeeded in driving the Separatist forces out of Mon Cala. Following the [[Battle of Mon Cala|battle]], Lee-Char was [[Coronation of Lee-Char|crowned]] as the new king and restored peace between the Mon Calamari and Quarren.<ref name="Prisoners">{{TCW|Prisoners}}</ref>

[[File:White_Calamari.png|thumb|left|200px|A pair of Mon Calamari alongside Rebel troopers]]
At the end of the Clone Wars, with the Jedi exterminated and Palpatine's rise to power as Emperor of the newly formed [[Galactic Empire]], he subjugated and enslaved the Mon Calamari and occupied Mon Cala. In response, the Mon Calamari threw their weight behind the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]] and played an important role in supplying warships to the [[Rebel Alliance Navy|Alliance Fleet]].<ref name="DB MonCal" />

After years of peace a [[First Order-Resistance War|war]] broke out between the [[First Order]] and the [[Resistance]]. After the [[Battle of Crait]], [[General]] [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa]] [[Mission to Mon Cala|led]] her depleted Resistance to Mon Cala to rally the Mon Calamari people to her cause and get much needed Mon Calamari cruisers.<ref name="Allegiance 1">[[Allegiance 1|''Allegiance'' 1]]</ref> [[King]] [[Ech-Char]] was reluctant to offer the cruisers at first,<ref name="Allegiance 2">[[Allegiance 2|''Allegiance'' 2]]</ref> but agreed after they were betrayed and the First Order took over.<ref name="Allegiance 4" /> Following the lead of [[Aftab Ackbar]], the [[Mon Cala fleet]] joined the rest of the Resistance and helped with the rebuilding of the [[Resistance navy]].<ref name="Allegiance 4">[[Allegiance 4|''Allegiance'' 4]]</ref>

==Mon Calamari in the galaxy==
[[File:AckbarBridgeCrew-BTMF24.png|thumb|right|300px|Several Mon Calamari, including Gial Ackbar, aboard the ''Home One'']]
Notable Mon Calamari included the Rebel Alliance [[Admiral]]s Gial Ackbar<ref name="Episode VI" /> and Raddus,<ref name="ROUVG">''[[Star Wars: Rogue One: The Ultimate Visual Guide]]''</ref> Resistance Colonel Aftab Ackbar,<ref name="Aftab Databank">{{Databank|aftab-ackbar|Aftab Ackbar}}</ref> Mon Calamari royals Yos Kolina and Lee-Char,<ref name="Water War" /> and the engineer [[Quarrie]], who built the first [[A/SF-01 B-wing starfighter|B-wing starfighters]] for the rebellion.<ref name="WotM" /> The Mon Calamari also produced force sensitives including [[Ephru Shinn]],<ref name="LOTJ" /> [[Eekar Oki]],<ref name="Grievous Intrigue">{{TCW|Grievous Intrigue}}</ref> and [[Nahdar Vebb]].<ref name="Lair of Grievous" /> A Mon Calamari named [[Karbin]] served as a [[commander]] during the Clone Wars until his ship was lost, resulting in him becoming a [[cyborg]].<ref name="Darth Vader 6">[[Darth Vader (2015) 6|''Darth Vader'' (2015) 6]]</ref> During the last days of the Clone Wars, several Mon Calamari musicians performed the ''[[Squid Lake]]'' at the [[Galaxies Opera House]] in [[Coruscant]].<ref name="Episode III" />

==Behind the scenes==
Mon Calamari first appeared in the [[1983]] film [[Star Wars: Episode VI Return of the Jedi|''Star Wars'': Episode VI ''Return of the Jedi'']], the third and final installment of the ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[original trilogy]].<ref name="Episode VI" /> They were first identified as Mon Calamarian by the [[2016]] [[Star Wars video games|game]] ''[[Star Wars Rebels: Chopper Chase]]''.<ref name="Chopper Chase">{{Disney|subdomain=lol|url=games/star-wars-rebels-chopper-chase|text=Star Wars Rebels: Chopper Chase|int=Star Wars Rebels: Chopper Chase|nolive=1}}</ref>

Creature artist [[Phil Tippett]] named the species after a [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Squid_as_food calamari] salad he ate for [[Foodstuff|lunch]] one [[Standard day|day]].<ref name="Much to Learn" />

